Specular patch to jpegxl-src 0.12.0 (src/lib.rs): building libjxl natively on Windows.

What it changes
  1. Ninja and clang-cl. Upstream always configures libjxl on Windows with the Visual Studio
     generator and `-T ClangCL`. When the cmake generator is Ninja (`CMAKE_GENERATOR=Ninja`, or
     one of the target-specific variants the cmake crate reads), the toolset is not requested
     and CMAKE_C_COMPILER / CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER are set to the clang-cl.exe found on PATH;
     without that, the cmake crate would set them to cl.exe. The generator variables are also
     declared as rerun-if-env-changed. With no Ninja generator, the generator and toolset are
     upstream's.
  2. C runtime. Upstream sets CMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY=MultiThreaded (static CRT, /MT) on
     every Windows build. Rust links the dynamic CRT (/MD) unless `+crt-static`, so the runtime
     now follows the target's crt-static feature: MultiThreadedDLL by default.
  3. Stale build folders. A CMake build folder configured (or left half-configured) by the
     other Windows generator is removed before the build.

Why
  1. `-T ClangCL` needs Visual Studio's optional "MSBuild support for LLVM (clang-cl) toolset"
     component; a standalone LLVM install does not provide it, and the configure step fails with
     MSB8020. With Ninja only clang-cl and ninja are needed.
  2. `/Zl` drops the default-library directives, but MSVC's STL headers still record the runtime
     in every C++ object (`#pragma detect_mismatch`), so linking libjxl's /MT objects with the
     /MD C code of other crates (mimalloc, libwebp, UnRAR) fails with LNK2038 'RuntimeLibrary'.
  3. The cmake crate skips configuring whenever CMakeCache.txt exists, so after switching
     generators (or after a failed Visual Studio configure, then installing clang-cl and Ninja)
     the old folder would be reused and fail again until `cargo clean -p gamut-jxl-sys`.

The `src/` directory is the published crate's with this patch applied; it is kept here as the
record of the change.

--- a/src/lib.rs
